# Copy this to a real environment file for LOCAL work. Never commit a filled-in copy.
#
# 🔴 THE LOCAL PATH NEEDS NONE OF THESE. `npm test`, `npm run eval`, `npm run call`,
# `npm run mock`, `npm run doctor` and `npm run verify` all run against the in-repo mock backend
# and hold no credential at all. Run `npm run doctor` for a reading of your own machine rather
# than a claim in a comment.
#
# ⚠️ Two commands legitimately ask for something before any real call exists:
# `npm run mint-token` needs VENUE_CALL_SECRET (a literal you invent), and the first tuning
# measurement needs GEMINI_API_KEY. Neither is a defect. See docs/LIMITS.md §9.
#
# The variables are in classes and the class is stated on each one, because "required" with no
# qualifier is what previously made a service refuse to boot on a laptop that needed nothing.

# ── class 1: has a working default, override only to point at a real backend ─────────────────
# Where the CreatoRain backend lives.
#   the in-repo mock:            http://127.0.0.1:8788   (the default; `npm run mock` serves it)
#   platform-backend on a laptop: http://localhost:4400  (API_PORT defaults to 4400 in src/index.ts)
# CREATORAIN_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788

# Port the agent itself listens on. Only matters once there is a carrier webhook to receive.
# PORT=8787

# ── class 2: needed only to talk to a REAL platform-backend ──────────────────────────────────
# The signing key for the call-scoped capability token. It must match the backend's own
# VENUE_CALL_SECRET exactly; it is a shared literal, not a credential anybody issues.
#
# With it unset on the BACKEND the whole seam is dark and every route refuses `seam_disabled`.
# Locally, pick any throwaway string and set the same
# one on both processes: `npm run mint-token` will use it. Setting it on a DEPLOYED service is
# the repository owner's call, not yours.
# VENUE_CALL_SECRET=

# ── class 3: needed only for a REAL model session (the Gemini Live adapter) ──────────────────
# The conversational model. Nothing in this repo needs it until an actual Gemini Live session is
# opened; the reference agent, the harness, the eval and every test run without it.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Override the pinned model. Leave unset unless you are running a comparison — the pin and the
# reasoning behind it are in src/tuning/liveDefaults.ts, and an unreviewed model swap is the one
# change most likely to move latency by seconds.
# GEMINI_LIVE_MODEL=

# The INDEPENDENT transcriber used by the post-call fabrication check. Pinned to Google Cloud
# Speech-to-Text.
#
# Independent is the point: without a second transcriber the check reads only the model's own
# account of its own speech, which is the one witness that cannot contradict it.
# SPEECH_TO_TEXT_CREDENTIALS=

# ── class 4: ENGINEER-ONLY. An outside contributor never sets this ───────────────────────────
# A path to a plain-text list of REAL venue names, one per line, `#` for comments. When set,
# `npm run check:no-facts` also fails on any of those names in src/. The list itself lives OUTSIDE
# this repository and is NEVER committed — not here, not hashed, not in a fixture. A CreatoRain
# engineer holds it. Unset, every other no-facts rule still runs, and the venue rule still checks
# its invented control name. A path that cannot be read, or a list with no names, fails the run.
# CI sets it from a repository secret on every run except a fork's pull request.
# VENUE_NAME_LIST_FILE=
